A load, a source and a continuing service (@pe-service: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Electric-Power-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_6JR10ZVGMZ7GT4RRK7734JQ7WD", #source "../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR", #electrical-power-engineering "Electrical-vocabulary-ports-nodes-and-equipment.lingua#r_4EGYDJC4Z79BQZ6E7WDZX7P0VC") { r_2N87DRV5NA20MK2HE1XEC7PF1X
**Read:** [Introduction to Electric Power Systems — MIT 6.061](../sources/Introduction-to-Electric-Power-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_6JR10ZVGMZ7GT4RRK7734JQ7WD), the course introduction and source/conversion context; [Improving Motor and Drive System Performance — DOE](../sources/Improving-Motor-and-Drive-System-Performance-DOE.lingua#r_71MGTGWBE9B62SJ1GS6Y3W8MKR), complete introductory system overview.

An electrical load is part of a wider process. A pump needs torque across a speed range; a computer needs a supply within voltage, interruption and waveform limits. A power system must deliver the required function while managing losses, disturbances, changes and failure. Producing a rated number of watts in one test does not establish continuing service.

Draw source, conversion, distribution, load, return/earthing paths, protective devices, sensing/control and auxiliary supplies. Label boundaries and identify who operates and maintains each part. A normal power path and a fault-current path can be different. A control or trip system may depend on a battery even when its main generator is stopped.

Begin with a small documented low-energy system or a complete published case. State useful output, nominal and allowable conditions, duty, failure consequences and the evidence needed to show function. Add a chronological account of startup, normal operation, fault response, maintenance and restoration. This question will deepen through circuits, fields, machines, networks, dynamic models and physical tests. [Hephaestus](../../../Hephaestus.lingua#r_00000000000000000000002001) connects the material supply, tools, people and recurring work without turning every linked subject into a compulsory detour.

**Continue:** [Electrical vocabulary, ports, nodes and equipment](Electrical-vocabulary-ports-nodes-and-equipment.lingua#r_4EGYDJC4Z79BQZ6E7WDZX7P0VC).

